    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's a pretty dark way to put it. but i guess you're right. if the whole thing is just an accident of biology and physics, then any \"meaning\" we find is just a cope to avoid the reality of the void. why is there this constant, desperate social pressure to keep the subscription active, even when the service itself is broken and clearly isn't providing much value anymore? it feels like we're just being forced to endure for the sake of enduring.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
